{
  "title": "Posteromedial Tibial Bowing",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4057/posteromedial-tibial-bowing",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 26 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Posteromedial Tibial Bowing is a congenital condition thought to be a result of intrauterine positioning that typically presents with a calcaneovalgus foot deformity and leg length discrepancy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with xrays of the tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation for bowing deformity which usually spontaneously corrects over 5-7 years. If leg-length discrepancy develops, nonoperative or operative management may be indicated depending on the severity of the discrepancy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually involves middle and distal third of tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "no known genetic association",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**calcaneovalgus foot**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posteromedial bowing is often confused with calcaneovalgus foot, another condition caused by intrauterine positioning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the two conditions may occur together or independently of each other",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "presents at birth",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posteromedial bowing**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "apex of deformity is in the distal tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4057/images/cvf%20vs.%20postero%20medial%20bowing.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**calcaneovalgus** foot deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "apex of deformity is at the ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "will see posterior medial bowing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4057/images/Xray%20-%20AP%20-%20lat%20leg%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
